  "limitations": [
    "Private C correction fixes per-tile terminal search only; it has no regression qualification for every other Magic device class.",
    "All 24 Magic HBTs now connect C/B/E correctly, but 16 Nx2/Nx4 instances still lose multiplicity; ngspice() also omits the finite tap. This Magic device output remains rejected.",
    "Hybrid retains all native KLayout device/model/parameter tokens and the finite tap, and separately proves 73 wire conductors, 146 anchors, 73 R edges and full collapsed C matrix.",
    "Metal/via-only RC excludes intrinsic terminal distribution, metal-device coupling, substrate spreading and RF calibration. This is not full-bank PEX or PHY adoption.",
    "First flattened geometry controls are confounded by a separate native KLayout orientation-dependent dimension swap. They are not accepted negative proof; hierarchy-preserving controls plus unchanged-clone positive are the accepted set.",
    "Native deck exits zero on several genuine mismatches; actual comparison/log status, exact census and database terminal/parameter binding decide acceptance.",
    "Reference points are explicit long-axis endpoints within the real pin shapes; failed short-axis anchor attempts retain killed/missing native nodes and remain rejected."
  ],
